course: dictionary
lesson: 9382
title: The word spotter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spotter is a person who watches out for something, often as a hobby. A train spotter writes down train numbers, and a bird spotter notes the birds they see. Spotters pay close attention, so they notice things other people miss.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «And remember a teacher can turn the bot into a lesson: find the three mistakes in its history answer, and you become an expert mistake-spotter.» The word mistake comes first, so a mistake-spotter is someone who finds mistakes. Try it: does "someone who finds mistakes" fit the sentence? It does.
explain: In sport, a spotter has a safety job. «Gymnastics is about control: flips are learned over months with a coach, spotters and thick mats, never from a video on the sofa.» Spotters stand by to catch you or help if you lose control, so the flip is safer.
fact: A spotter is a person who watches out for something, often as a hobby.
fact: A spotter can also watch for danger or an enemy and report it, such as a fire spotter.
fact: In gym and weightlifting, a spotter stands by to catch you or help if you lose control.
fact: «Mistake-spotter» and «pattern-spotter» are made by joining two words: the spotter finds the mistake or the pattern.
fact: Spotters need sharp eyes and careful attention, because they must notice things others miss.
exercise: «And remember... you become an expert mistake-spotter.» In that sentence, what is a mistake-spotter? | *Someone who finds mistakes | Someone who makes the most mistakes | A bot that writes history answers | A teacher who marks homework in red
exercise: «Gymnastics is about control: flips are learned... with a coach, spotters and thick mats.» What do spotters do in gymnastics? | They sell tickets to the competition | They clean the thick mats after training | They judge the score for each routine | *They stand by to catch or help you if you lose control
exercise: A train spotter in the UK notes down train numbers. What is a train spotter? | A person who fixes the railway tracks | *A person who watches trains as a hobby and notes what they see | A driver who controls the train
test: «That is AI at its best: a patient pattern-spotter helping people do something they could not do alone.» What is a pattern-spotter? | Someone who sews clothes | Someone who paints patterns on walls | *Someone who notices patterns | A teacher who gives out patterns
test: In wartime, what is a fire spotter or aircraft spotter? | A person who puts out fires with water | A pilot who flies in the air show | A soldier who fires the big guns | *Someone who watches for danger, such as enemy planes, and reports it
exam: Which word means a person who watches out for something and notices what others miss? | Spot | Spotted | Spotless | *Spotter
